==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Noun usage possibly from the adjective {{m|en|scurvy}} influenced by or a variant of {{m|en|scurfy}}. Took on meaning of {{cog|nl|scheurbuik}}, {{cog|fr|scorbut||scurvy}}, possibly from {{der|en|non|skyrbjúgr}}, {{m|non|skyr||sour milk}} + {{m|non|bjúgr||swelling, tumour}}, from the verb {{m|non|bjúga|t=to bend}}, whence {{cog|is|skyrbjúgur||scurvy}}, {{cog|da|skørbug||scurvy}} and {{cog|sv|skörbjugg||scurvy}}.

Compare {{cog|de|Scharbock}}, {{cog|la-lat|scorbutus}}. More at {{l|en|sour}}, {{l|en|bow}}.

Or, equivalent to {{suffix|en|scurf|y|t1=flakes on the surface of the skin}}.<ref>{{R:Lexico}}</ref>

